1
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:52,990
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:56,010
[Episode 23]

3
00:00:58,850 --> 00:01:00,530
Dried persimmons!

4
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:13,010
You're supposed to
chew the prawn crisp candy.

5
00:01:13,010 --> 00:01:14,430
You're sucking on it.

6
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:15,280
Just tasting it.

7
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,170
What about this?

8
00:01:16,190 --> 00:01:17,450
You want some of this?

9
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:18,350
Wait, wait a moment.

10
00:01:18,350 --> 00:01:19,950
-I'll take a walk around, then come back.
-Yeah, take a walk.

11
00:01:19,950 --> 00:01:20,850
I'll take a walk and come back.

12
00:01:22,350 --> 00:01:23,360
Lifting you up high.

13
00:01:24,090 --> 00:01:25,090
Lifting you up high.

14
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:26,930
Your head is all covered.

15
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:30,900
Flying up.

16
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:32,180
Look at your face. Like a little kitten.

17
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:35,000
Our Qianqian is a little kitten.

18
00:01:35,870 --> 00:01:36,680
Little kitten.

19
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:44,789
It's so sweet! Come!

20
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:50,650
I want to eat popcorn.

21
00:01:50,650 --> 00:01:52,100
It's so awesome.

22
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:53,930
-So awesome.
-So awesome.

23
00:01:53,930 --> 00:01:56,140
-You can speak Northeast dialect so soon.
-Listen to that.

24
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:57,479
You can't eat that stuff.

25
00:01:57,479 --> 00:01:58,570
It's full of lead.

26
00:01:58,570 --> 00:01:59,810
If you eat too much, you'll get dumb.

27
00:02:00,590 --> 00:02:02,040
We're smart enough.

28
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:02,640
Right?

29
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:03,840
We're not afraid of getting dumb.

30
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:04,290
Let's go.

31
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:05,570
-Where are you going?
-I'll take you to eat popcorn.

32
00:02:06,150 --> 00:02:07,090
You're spoiling her.

33
00:02:08,410 --> 00:02:09,770
Here we go, popcorn!

34
00:02:09,930 --> 00:02:10,840
-Let's go!
-Slow down.

35
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:11,410
You're

36
00:02:11,410 --> 00:02:13,210
acting wildly all day.

37
00:02:13,210 --> 00:02:13,780
Slow down!

38
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:17,950
Let's go buy popcorn.

39
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:20,860
Sir.

40
00:02:21,210 --> 00:02:22,360
How much is this popcorn?

41
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:23,210
Fifty cents.

42
00:02:23,210 --> 00:02:24,280
Fifty cents? Okay.

43
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:29,800
Popcorn.

44
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:30,280
Let's go.

45
00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:32,270
What else do you want to eat?

46
00:02:32,430 --> 00:02:33,210
Good for you.

47
00:02:33,210 --> 00:02:34,210
Jump. Let's go.

48
00:02:35,579 --> 00:02:36,970
Qianqian, look at this.

49
00:02:36,970 --> 00:02:38,130
Does it look like Juan?

50
00:02:39,380 --> 00:02:40,410
Does it look like Juan?

51
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:41,880
Does it look like Juan? Poke it.

52
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,030
Does it look like Juan?

53
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:45,620
Hello, sir.

54
00:02:45,620 --> 00:02:46,710
I'd like two ears of corn.

55
00:02:46,710 --> 00:02:47,300
Okay.

56
00:02:49,060 --> 00:02:49,810
Juan.

57
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:51,810
Liu Yang

58
00:02:51,810 --> 00:02:54,140
is already married, isn't he?

59
00:02:54,390 --> 00:02:56,700
You've done enough as a sister.

60
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:58,370
You should start thinking about yourself.

61
00:02:58,670 --> 00:03:01,530
I think this family of three
is really great.

62
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:04,530
I don't have the luck
to enjoy a peaceful life.

63
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:07,180
These two are enough
for me to worry about.

64
00:03:07,970 --> 00:03:09,870
I see you alone all day,

65
00:03:09,870 --> 00:03:11,750
braving the wind and rain.

66
00:03:11,750 --> 00:03:14,110
It would be nice to have someone
to talk to when you get home,

67
00:03:14,140 --> 00:03:15,870
someone who cares about you.

68
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:18,090
I think this young man He

69
00:03:18,090 --> 00:03:19,310
is quite reliable.

70
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,780
Why don't you get him to come to Tiecheng?

71
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:23,530
Your stall—

72
00:03:23,530 --> 00:03:24,400
Go back quickly.

73
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:26,010
Your sunflower seeds
are being grabbed by people.

74
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:27,370
No more chatting.

75
00:03:27,370 --> 00:03:28,150
I'm leaving.

76
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:30,310
-Go on!
-Remember to invite me to your wedding.

77
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:31,400
Stop it.

78
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:38,630
Thanks.

79
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:41,260
Who wants fried cakes?

80
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:42,990
Juan.

81
00:03:43,030 --> 00:03:43,810
Juan.

82
00:03:43,810 --> 00:03:45,630
Let's go find Juan.

83
00:03:45,630 --> 00:03:46,880
You're back.

84
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,400
Who was it that was asking for

85
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:50,910
freshly fried cakes a couple of days ago?

86
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:52,540
Juan.

87
00:03:52,570 --> 00:03:53,850
Juan.

88
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:54,530
Wait,

89
00:03:55,190 --> 00:03:55,710
why did you

90
00:03:56,090 --> 00:03:57,370
buy so many?

91
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,560
Where did you buy these?

92
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:02,240
Is it the one at the east end?

93
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:03,960
How much?

94
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:04,920
That old man's so greedy.

95
00:04:05,090 --> 00:04:06,410
Qianqian and I bargained hard.

96
00:04:06,410 --> 00:04:07,410
Right, Qianqian?

97
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:11,280
Alright then.

98
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:13,310
Let's go back
and I'll stew some fish for you.

99
00:04:13,310 --> 00:04:15,410
I want stewed tofu.

100
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:16,680
Stewed tofu.

101
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:18,600
-She wants stewed tofu.
-Stewed fish is good.

102
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:20,120
Then we need soybean paste.

103
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:21,990
The smellier the paste,
the better it tastes.

104
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:24,220
Okay, we've got soybean paste at home.

105
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:25,890
Look at how much you two bought.

106
00:04:25,890 --> 00:04:27,040
If there was a pile of
warm shit on the street,

107
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:28,190
you two would have to taste it.

108
00:04:28,190 --> 00:04:28,890
Let's go.

109
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:32,780
She said we'd eat warm shit.

110
00:04:34,310 --> 00:04:35,330
Let's go home.

111
00:04:36,070 --> 00:04:36,920
Let's go.

112
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:39,540
Let's go.

113
00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:40,950
Let's go home and eat stewed tofu.

114
00:04:40,950 --> 00:04:41,420
Let's go.

115
00:04:43,980 --> 00:04:44,890
Bye, sir.

116
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:54,890
Easy.

117
00:04:54,890 --> 00:04:56,120
You might cut your hand.

118
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:58,030
You see, I eat so well every day.

119
00:04:58,190 --> 00:04:59,300
What if I can't have this anymore

120
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:00,870
in the future and crave it?

121
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:02,980
Why does it sound like

122
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:04,830
you're enjoying yourself
too much to leave?

123
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:06,060
Deng said

124
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:07,890
you're doing great in their arrest team.

125
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:09,130
They don't want you to leave

126
00:05:09,130 --> 00:05:10,310
and want to keep you.

127
00:05:16,170 --> 00:05:18,170
I forgot to pay you
for this month's meals.

128
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:24,560
Why are you giving me so much?

129
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:25,870
Didn't we agree you'd pay
at the end of the month?

130
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:27,240
Are you paying for the whole year?

131
00:05:27,830 --> 00:05:28,770
Just take it.

132
00:05:28,770 --> 00:05:30,270
Keeping this allowance
doesn't do me any good.

133
00:05:32,450 --> 00:05:33,720
Who'd complain about
having too much money?

134
00:05:34,159 --> 00:05:35,060
I'm a penny-pincher.

135
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:35,930
Money only comes in, never goes out.

136
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:39,010
What do you want to eat tomorrow?

137
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:41,330
Tomorrow—

138
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:43,310
How about we eat out?

139
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:44,930
Are we made of money?

140
00:05:45,510 --> 00:05:46,890
Or do you think my cooking's no good?

141
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:48,120
No.

142
00:05:48,510 --> 00:05:49,450
I've been here all these days

143
00:05:49,450 --> 00:05:50,930
and haven't properly eaten out.

144
00:05:51,270 --> 00:05:54,720
I want to eat out and have something good.

145
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:56,540
Didn't we agree?

146
00:05:56,540 --> 00:05:57,920
No talking during hide-and-seek.

147
00:05:57,920 --> 00:05:59,430
Why did you expose yourself again?

148
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:05,010
Look.

149
00:06:05,010 --> 00:06:06,450
Lately we've been

150
00:06:07,630 --> 00:06:08,950
either busy investigating cases

151
00:06:09,130 --> 00:06:10,160
or busy with the wedding.

152
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,220
We've been so busy

153
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:12,770
that I haven't treated you
and Liu Yang to a meal.

154
00:06:13,370 --> 00:06:15,370
Why are you suddenly being so polite?

155
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:20,120
Then it's settled.

156
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:21,510
You pick a date.

157
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:22,740
Ask him out then.

158
00:06:24,370 --> 00:06:25,070
Okay.

159
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:28,950
Here are two more.

160
00:06:29,890 --> 00:06:30,370
Done.

161
00:06:32,830 --> 00:06:34,470
Let me show you what I can do.

162
00:06:34,670 --> 00:06:35,600
Go away. Let me do it.

163
00:06:38,070 --> 00:06:39,530
The oil needs to be hot.

164
00:06:39,870 --> 00:06:40,870
Add some MSG.

165
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:43,070
Your MSG...

166
00:06:43,070 --> 00:06:43,720
You're no good at this.

167
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:44,630
Move aside. Move.

168
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:45,830
-You do it.
-What is this?

169
00:06:46,570 --> 00:06:47,470
You're good.

170
00:06:54,170 --> 00:06:56,620
[Female: Great Post Earth]
[Male: Willow Wood] [Yin-Shen Clash]

171
00:07:00,270 --> 00:07:01,270
Your...

172
00:07:01,270 --> 00:07:01,620
Look at you,

173
00:07:01,620 --> 00:07:02,430
tsking

174
00:07:02,430 --> 00:07:03,570
and sighing.

175
00:07:04,620 --> 00:07:05,890
You insisted on looking at it.

176
00:07:06,370 --> 00:07:08,240
And now you're acting like this.

177
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:09,690
What's wrong?

178
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:11,930
It's fate.

179
00:07:12,370 --> 00:07:13,600
You two are destined.

180
00:07:14,450 --> 00:07:15,420
But it's just t-this...

181
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:16,770
this zodiac sign.

182
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:17,480
You see.

183
00:07:17,740 --> 00:07:19,060
You were born in the Year of the Monkey.

184
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:20,600
He was born in the Year of the Tiger.

185
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:22,370
Isn't that a zodiac clash?

186
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:24,390
Yin-Shen clash.

187
00:07:24,570 --> 00:07:25,240
What?

188
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:27,390
Yin-Shen clash.

189
00:07:27,390 --> 00:07:28,270
Yin and Shen?

190
00:07:28,270 --> 00:07:30,500
Right. When things are good,

191
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:31,630
you attract each other,

192
00:07:31,630 --> 00:07:32,720
and you'll be super clingy.

193
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:33,980
You... You'll be...

194
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:35,659
just... just like that.

195
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:36,310
Stop it.

196
00:07:36,310 --> 00:07:38,360
But when you fight,

197
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:40,230
you almost tear the roof off.

198
00:07:40,570 --> 00:07:41,390
You know?

199
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,220
And then look at the birth chart.

200
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:47,330
You're Great Post Earth,

201
00:07:47,330 --> 00:07:49,060
and he's Willow Wood.

202
00:07:49,390 --> 00:07:50,630
How should I put it?

203
00:07:50,630 --> 00:07:53,330
You're like the landlady
of a roadside inn,

204
00:07:54,450 --> 00:07:55,659
and he's just a singer

205
00:07:55,659 --> 00:07:57,890
who came here to perform.

206
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:01,500
You—you were drawn to his talent.

207
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:03,000
You can really warm him up.

208
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:03,750
You know?

209
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:06,060
But the problem is, can...

210
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:08,950
can you keep him?

211
00:08:09,190 --> 00:08:09,890
That's the thing.

212
00:08:14,190 --> 00:08:15,240
Stop dawdling.

213
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:16,830
Just get straight to the point.

214
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:19,290
Why do you always pull this act?

215
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,620
No, if you two...

216
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:22,870
Let me put it this way,

217
00:08:22,870 --> 00:08:24,370
if you had met five years earlier,

218
00:08:24,620 --> 00:08:25,770
you'd both be young and hot-blooded.

219
00:08:25,770 --> 00:08:26,240
Let me tell you,

220
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:27,450
you'd fight—

221
00:08:27,450 --> 00:08:28,420
you'd fight fiercely,

222
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:29,660
and you'd definitely end up divorced.

223
00:08:29,660 --> 00:08:30,670
Really?

224
00:08:30,830 --> 00:08:33,240
But you met now.

225
00:08:34,610 --> 00:08:36,620
The timing isn't quite right.

226
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:39,659
You two have to...

227
00:08:41,929 --> 00:08:43,950
It's best to wait five years.

228
00:08:44,220 --> 00:08:46,120
Things will be stable then.

229
00:08:46,170 --> 00:08:47,550
So there's no chance now?

230
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:54,470
There... There is a chance,

231
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:55,860
but whether it works or not

232
00:08:55,860 --> 00:08:57,510
depends on what he thinks.

233
00:08:57,940 --> 00:08:59,240
Oh, come on.

234
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:00,700
You're just making wild guesses here.

235
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:02,550
Nothing good has happened since he came.

236
00:09:02,550 --> 00:09:04,120
Cases one after another.

237
00:09:04,890 --> 00:09:06,010
Besides, he never said

238
00:09:06,010 --> 00:09:06,720
he was staying.

239
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:08,270
Once the case is done, he has to leave.

240
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:10,270
I told you I won't listen.

241
00:09:10,270 --> 00:09:11,740
You're just blabbering here.

242
00:09:11,740 --> 00:09:13,250
I thought you had
something serious to tell me.

243
00:09:13,390 --> 00:09:13,840
It'll work.

244
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:15,270
-I must be bored, listening to you here.
-Trust me.

245
00:09:15,270 --> 00:09:17,440
Let's... Let's wait and see in five years.

246
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:18,670
Qianqian, let's go.

247
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:21,000
Okay.

248
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,010
I got it.

249
00:09:22,530 --> 00:09:23,360
Okay.

250
00:09:23,750 --> 00:09:24,500
See you later.

251
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:25,050
Okay, bye.

252
00:09:26,770 --> 00:09:28,820
The squad called for backup.

253
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:30,510
They said they caught

254
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:32,580
a middleman trafficking wild animals.

255
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:33,530
I'll go take a look.

256
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:35,240
Sign this for me later.

257
00:09:35,510 --> 00:09:35,870
Okay.

258
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:39,840
Juan is really a big deal now.

259
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:42,050
He Liang has to report to her
before going on duty.

260
00:09:42,150 --> 00:09:42,890
If he doesn't report,

261
00:09:42,890 --> 00:09:44,630
she won't cook dinner for him.

262
00:09:44,630 --> 00:09:45,740
Stop talking nonsense!

263
00:09:45,990 --> 00:09:47,530
I'm rushed off my feet all day.

264
00:10:07,470 --> 00:10:12,440
[Liu Yang: Major Suspect]

265
00:10:12,810 --> 00:10:14,740
[Liu Yang and Portrait]
[Striking Resemblance]

266
00:10:14,770 --> 00:10:16,650
[Liu Yang Chen Hong] [Driver]

267
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:23,600
[Forest Farm Fire: Three Dead]

268
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:25,750
[Zhao Changyou Died; Liu Yang
Returned to Tiecheng;  Date Unknown]

269
00:10:33,350 --> 00:10:35,160
[Zhao Changyou Died; Liu Yang
Returned to Tiecheng; Date Unknown]

270
00:10:35,370 --> 00:10:37,600
[Phone Notebook]

271
00:10:44,890 --> 00:10:45,580
Juan!

272
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,380
Juan, what's wrong?

273
00:10:49,770 --> 00:10:51,010
Didn't you hear me calling you?

274
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:52,740
What's up?

275
00:10:54,220 --> 00:10:55,000
Are you mad?

276
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:01,980
Let me tell you.

277
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:03,840
I hate people who beat around the bush.

278
00:11:04,250 --> 00:11:04,960
You're a grown man.

279
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:05,750
Why are you being so sneaky?

280
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:06,500
If you suspect Liu Yang,

281
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:07,870
just take him to the interrogation room.

282
00:11:07,870 --> 00:11:08,720
Why did you invite us to dinner

283
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:09,770
and put on this show?

284
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:11,510
I treated you to good food and drinks,

285
00:11:11,510 --> 00:11:12,620
and it was wasted on a dog!

286
00:11:30,700 --> 00:11:32,320
You're being too harsh.

287
00:11:33,170 --> 00:11:34,850
Besides, what did dogs ever do to you?

288
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,500
Animals are better than people.

289
00:11:36,770 --> 00:11:37,340
Right.

290
00:11:37,910 --> 00:11:39,250
Don't be a human in your next life.

291
00:11:41,770 --> 00:11:43,670
Do I have no reason to suspect him?

292
00:11:44,510 --> 00:11:46,200
Just because he's your brother—

293
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:47,670
There's an obvious lead,

294
00:11:47,670 --> 00:11:48,690
and I-I just ignore it?

295
00:11:49,330 --> 00:11:51,030
So you're suspecting me now?

296
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:52,320
The timing of his return

297
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:53,940
is pretty close to
when Zhao Changyou died.

298
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:55,890
I really didn't expect that. So what?

299
00:11:56,170 --> 00:11:57,250
You think I'm covering for him?

300
00:11:58,630 --> 00:12:00,820
You? You act like a mother hen all day,

301
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:01,240
protecting him.

302
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:02,200
What do you expect me to think?

303
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:08,100
So you've been
suspecting us all along, huh?

304
00:12:12,750 --> 00:12:14,000
I just have one question.

305
00:12:14,580 --> 00:12:16,260
After the forest farm fire,

306
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:17,430
he came back to Tiecheng.

307
00:12:17,770 --> 00:12:19,180
Why didn't he come find you first?

308
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:22,420
Is it possible

309
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:24,680
that because his job
made it easy to transport goods,

310
00:12:24,820 --> 00:12:26,320
he teamed up with Zhao Changyou?

311
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:29,420
He actually went back
to Tiecheng to see Zhao Changyou.

312
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:30,940
Didn't the restaurant owner say?

313
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,080
It was a young man.

314
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:32,840
Earlier you said

315
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:34,500
Liu Yang killed Li Dewu for Chen Hong.

316
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:36,240
How's he suddenly
teaming up with Zhao Changyou?

317
00:12:36,620 --> 00:12:38,250
They definitely
have an improper relationship.

318
00:12:38,250 --> 00:12:39,240
Didn't you see it?

319
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:49,930
I know.

320
00:12:50,670 --> 00:12:52,370
In your heart, Liu Yang is just

321
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:53,610
an ignorant kid.

322
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:56,390
But do you really know him?

323
00:12:56,410 --> 00:12:58,360
Do you know what he does every day?

324
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:02,500
How did he survive

325
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:03,440
that fire?

326
00:13:03,510 --> 00:13:05,390
And how did he become Chen Hong's driver?

327
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:07,270
In just two months,

328
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:09,410
he went from being penniless

329
00:13:09,870 --> 00:13:10,830
to having a car,

330
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:12,050
a job,

331
00:13:12,220 --> 00:13:13,420
and even a wife.

332
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:14,960
How did he do that?

333
00:13:21,250 --> 00:13:22,270
I'll be honest with you.

334
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:23,940
If it really is Liu Yang,

335
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:25,440
I shouldn't have gotten so close to you.

336
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:29,030
And telling you all this
would be for nothing.

337
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:32,670
If it really is Liu Yang,

338
00:13:33,550 --> 00:13:35,170
I'll personally cuff him
and take him to the station.

339
00:13:39,250 --> 00:13:41,830
Then do you dare let him
go to Gang's Diner

340
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:43,290
and let the owner identify him?

341
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:45,340
Fine, let's go!

342
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:47,220
What, you think I'm afraid of you?

343
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:49,530
What if it's not him?

344
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:54,460
Whatever you say.

345
00:13:54,830 --> 00:13:55,770
It's up to you.

346
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:57,640
You have to kowtow and apologize to me!

347
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:01,740
Deal.

348
00:14:06,650 --> 00:14:07,340
Don't be mad.

349
00:14:07,340 --> 00:14:08,410
You look so pitiful.

350
00:14:16,130 --> 00:14:16,870
Hello, Mr. Liu.

351
00:14:19,340 --> 00:14:20,120
Yang.

352
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:22,540
Have you had lunch?

353
00:14:22,650 --> 00:14:23,370
Let's eat together.

354
00:14:26,130 --> 00:14:27,770
I was thinking of running some errands.

355
00:14:27,890 --> 00:14:29,100
Maybe next time.

356
00:14:31,530 --> 00:14:32,460
What are you busy with?

357
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:35,200
Your sister was craving some pork stew.

358
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:36,620
We just happened to stroll by here.

359
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:37,290
If you

360
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:39,080
are free, join us.

361
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:39,870
Forget it.

362
00:14:39,870 --> 00:14:40,770
Forget it.

363
00:14:40,770 --> 00:14:41,790
Another day. I've got

364
00:14:41,790 --> 00:14:42,840
something pretty important.

365
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,370
Well, if you've got stuff to do, go ahead.

366
00:14:44,370 --> 00:14:45,860
Come find us when you're done.

367
00:14:46,290 --> 00:14:47,670
We'll wait for you at Yuhong Square.

368
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:49,370
I just don't get

369
00:14:49,370 --> 00:14:50,980
what you're busy with all day.

370
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:52,940
You get a wife
and forget your sister, huh?

371
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:56,340
I don't know what you like to eat.

372
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:58,750
I heard this restaurant is pretty good.

373
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:14,240
You don't like it?
Let's go somewhere else.

374
00:15:15,770 --> 00:15:16,610
Why change?

375
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:17,870
This one's fine.

376
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:22,270
Welcome.

377
00:15:35,870 --> 00:15:36,600
What are you staring at?

378
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:37,770
Let's order.

379
00:15:39,340 --> 00:15:40,820
Well, what can I get for you three?

380
00:15:41,510 --> 00:15:42,820
Sir, how about this?

381
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:44,460
We'll have some

382
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:47,220
cabbage, bean sprouts, peanuts,

383
00:15:47,390 --> 00:15:50,050
jellyfish with scallions,
twice-cooked pork,

384
00:15:50,250 --> 00:15:51,820
and pickled cabbage dumplings.

385
00:15:58,890 --> 00:15:59,820
Anything else?

386
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:03,290
That's enough.

387
00:16:08,220 --> 00:16:09,320
Sir, just tell me straight.

388
00:16:09,660 --> 00:16:11,200
Was he the one
who came with Zhao Changyou?

389
00:16:31,720 --> 00:16:32,940
It really wasn't him.

390
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Well, watermelons and winter melons
are both melons,

391
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,390
but they are completely different.

392
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:40,620
Right?

393
00:16:42,020 --> 00:16:43,470
Are you sure it wasn't him?

394
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:44,550
Officer.

395
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:46,560
It's been over two months.

396
00:16:46,910 --> 00:16:48,130
I really can't remember.

397
00:16:54,250 --> 00:16:55,650
I wondered why you were looking for me.

398
00:16:56,010 --> 00:16:57,620
If you've got something to say,
just say it.

399
00:16:57,980 --> 00:16:59,260
There's no need for all this.

400
00:16:59,370 --> 00:16:59,960
Right?

401
00:17:06,750 --> 00:17:07,589
Cook everything on the menu for me.

402
00:17:08,170 --> 00:17:08,819
He's paying.

403
00:17:20,940 --> 00:17:21,450
Chopsticks.
